{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor path in [\n    '/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/15/prompt.md',\n    '/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/15/des.md',\n]:\n    print(f'FILE: {path}')\n    text = Path(path).read_text()\n    lines = text.splitlines()\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines[:220], start=1):\n        print(f'{i:4}: {line}')\n    print()\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"FILE: /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/15/prompt.md\n   1: 你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n   2: \n   3: 每个参考题描述包含：\n   4: - `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n   5: - `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n   6: - `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n   7: - `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n   8: \n   9: 参考题目如下：\n  10: <reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"0934a4d8\" lines=\"75-90\">\n  11: <description>\n  12: Reveal the rectangular patch hidden by the solid marker using the grid's reflection symmetries.\n  13: \n  14: Input structure:\n  15: - A square colored pattern with one solid rectangular marker color occluding a patch.\n  16: - The visible pattern has horizontal and vertical reflection symmetry on a large lower/right strip.\n  17: - The top and left outer strips also expose transpose counterparts for cells not recoverable by those reflections.\n  18: \n  19: Rule:\n  20: - Find the unique color whose full extent is a solid rectangle; this rectangle is the output region.\n  21: - Infer the reflected strip start as the smallest row/column offset whose lower/right strips are mirror-consistent, ignoring marker pixels.\n  22: - For each marker pixel, copy the unique non-marker value in its horizontal/vertical reflection orbit; if that orbit is entirely hidden in the outer strip, use the transposed top/left-strip counterpart.\n  23: \n  24: Key insight:\n  25: The marker is not part of the pattern; it covers a missing rectangle whose cells are still determined by the visible mirror or transpose copies elsewhere in the grid.\n  26: </description>\n  27: </reference_puzzle>\n  28: \n  29: <reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"18447a8d\" lines=\"33-48\">\n  30: <description>\n  31: Move each right-side colored shape into the left slot whose template color is its exact complement.\n  32: \n  33: Input structure:\n  34: - The grid has two equal-width slots separated by one background column.\n  35: - Non-background rows form horizontal bands separated by all-background rows.\n  36: - Each band has a shared template color in the left slot and one colored source shape in the right slot.\n  37: \n  38: Rule:\n  39: - For each band, define its destination shape as the cells in the left slot not occupied by the template color.\n  40: - Normalize every right-side source shape to right-slot coordinates and match it to the unique equal destination shape.\n  41: - Clear the original right-side source pixels and paint the matched left-slot complement with the source color.\n  42: \n  43: Key insight:\n  44: The right-side objects are not placed by row order; each one completes the unique left template whose missing cells have the same shape.\n  45: </description>\n  46: </reference_puzzle>\n  47: \n  48: <reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"880c1354\" lines=\"14-28\">\n  49: <description>\n  50: Recolor the separated outer regions by rotating their colors one step clockwise around the yellow-orange divider.\n  51: \n  52: Input structure:\n  53: - The grid contains a fixed yellow/orange divider structure.\n  54: - All other colors form separated 4-connected monochrome regions around that divider.\n  55: \n  56: Rule:\n  57: - Leave the yellow and orange pixels unchanged.\n  58: - Sort the non-divider regions by their centroid angle around the divider centroid in screen-coordinate clockwise order.\n  59: - Each region keeps its cells and receives the color of the previous region in that cyclic order.\n  60: \n  61: Key insight:\n  62: - The objects do not move; only the color labels cycle through the spatial order of the regions around the divider.\n  63: </description>\n  64: </reference_puzzle>\n  65: \n  66: <reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"97c75046\" lines=\"88-107\">\n  67: <description>\n  68: Move the single marker to the endpoint reached by sliding along the obstacle contour.\n  69: \n  70: Input structure:\n  71: - A dominant background color fills the canvas.\n  72: - One single-pixel marker sits away from a connected obstacle region of the\n  73:   remaining color.\n  74: - The marker has exactly one horizontal or vertical sightline to the obstacle.\n  75: \n  76: Rule:\n  77: - Find the last background pixel before the obstacle along that sightline.\n  78: - From that pixel, try the two diagonal turns that continue around the\n  79:   obstacle boundary.\n  80: - Move the marker to the endpoint of the turn that remains 4-adjacent to the\n  81:   obstacle for the longest distance.\n  82: \n  83: Key insight:\n  84: The marker is not placed by distance to the obstacle; it first points to the\n  85: obstacle, then follows the visible outside contour until that contour segment ends.\n  86: </description>\n  87: </reference_puzzle>\n  88: \n  89: <reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e4888269\" lines=\"67-88\">\n  90: <description>\n  91: Recolor every target pixel by following the ordered two-column substitution legend.\n  92: \n  93: Input structure\n  94: - A dominant background surrounds one multicolor vertical legend: a connected,\n  95:   fully filled two-column block with one color pair per row.\n  96: - Other non-background pixels or objects are the targets; divider or frame\n  97:   pixels are ordinary target-side structure that remain unchanged unless their\n  98:   color is rewritten by the legend.\n  99: \n 100: Rule\n 101: - Read the legend rows from top to bottom as substitutions from the left\n 102:   column color to the right column color.\n 103: - For each non-background pixel outside the legend, scan those rows in order;\n 104:   whenever the current color equals the row's left color, replace it with the\n 105:   row's right color and keep scanning lower rows.\n 106: - Leave the legend itself and background pixels unchanged.\n 107: \n 108: Key insight\n 109: - The same color may be rewritten multiple times, but only by substitutions\n 110:   that appear later in the vertical legend, so the row order is part of the\n 111:   symbol instruction.\n 112: </description>\n 113: </reference_puzzle>\n 114: \n 115: <reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5d588b4d\" lines=\"10-28\">\n 116: <description>\n 117: Expand the top-left horizontal bar into a wrapped sequence of increasing and decreasing foreground runs.\n 118: \n 119: Input structure:\n 120: - The grid has a background color and exactly one foreground color.\n 121: - All foreground pixels form one contiguous horizontal bar in the top row.\n 122: - The bar starts at the left edge; its length is the control value n.\n 123: \n 124: Rule:\n 125: - Build a one-dimensional sequence of foreground runs with lengths\n 126:   1, 2, ..., n, n-1, ..., 2, 1.\n 127: - Separate adjacent runs by one background pixel.\n 128: - Wrap the sequence row-major across the input width and pad the final row\n 129:   with background pixels.\n 130: \n 131: Key insight:\n 132: The output preserves the input width; the bar length controls the run-length\n 133: diamond, and the apparent 2D pattern is just that 1D sequence wrapped into rows.\n 134: </description>\n 135: </reference_puzzle>\n 136: \n 137: <reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"898e7135\" lines=\"7-20\">\n 138: <description>\n 139: Inflate a frame's hole-layout and fill each hole with its matching piece.\n 140: \n 141: Input structure:\n 142: - bg = most common color. Largest component is a monochrome frame enclosing bg holes.\n 143: - Outside pieces composed of k×k blocks; k = side of smallest solid square piece.\n 144: \n 145: Rule:\n 146: - Extract connected hole regions inside the frame as slots.\n 147: - Match each piece to a slot by comparing block-level shapes under rotation/flip.\n 148: - Output the layout scaled by k, with pieces placed in slots; frame color as background.\n 149: \n 150: Key insight: Pieces are k×k-block-scaled versions of holes; downsampling reveals shape matches under all 8 orientations.\n 151: </description>\n 152: </reference_puzzle>\n 153: \n 154: <reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"981571dc\" lines=\"6-19\">\n 155: <description>\n 156: Reconstruct a 4-way symmetric mosaic by filling missing (black) pixels.\n 157: \n 158: Input structure:\n 159: - A colored grid exhibiting bilateral symmetry along both a vertical and a horizontal axis.\n 160: - Some pixels are erased to color 0 (black), creating gaps in the pattern.\n 161: \n 162: Rule:\n 163: - Infer the vertical and horizontal reflection axes from the visible (non-zero) pixels.\n 164: - For each black pixel, recover its color from the mirrored position across either axis or both.\n 165: - When multiple mirrors yield candidates, use the majority color.\n 166: \n 167: Key insight: The reflection axes are not given — they must be deduced from the surviving pixels by finding the axes that best preserve the existing symmetry.\n 168: </description>\n 169: </reference_puzzle>\n 170: \n 171: <reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"abbfd121\" lines=\"56-74\">\n 172: <description>\n 173: Recover the repeating background pattern hidden under the largest solid rectangle.\n 174: \n 175: Input structure:\n 176: - The grid is covered by a small row/column periodic pattern.\n 177: - Several non-pattern colors form solid rectangular foreground objects that\n 178:   overwrite the pattern.\n 179: - The requested output region is the largest of those solid rectangles.\n 180: \n 181: Rule:\n 182: - Find every 4-connected monochromatic object whose bounding box is a filled\n 183:   rectangle with both dimensions greater than one.\n 184: - Treat those rectangles as masks, infer the smallest repeating tile that is\n 185:   consistent with all remaining visible pixels, and repaint the largest\n 186:   rectangle's coordinates with that tile.\n 187: \n 188: Key insight: The rectangle colors are occluders; the visible pixels outside\n 189: them are enough to reconstruct the original periodic background underneath.\n 190: </description>\n 191: </reference_puzzle>\n 192: \n 193: <reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"da6e95e5\" lines=\"70-81\">\n 194: <description>\n 195: Extract the central object from the marker cluster whose markers have the same color.\n 196: \n 197: Input structure\n 198: The grid has a dominant background and several clusters; each cluster has four\n 199: same-color corner marker objects around one central monochromatic object.\n 200: Rule\n 201: Find every central object enclosed by four aligned corner markers of one color,\n 202: then choose the unique one whose object color equals the marker color.\n 203: Key insight\n 204: The answer is not the largest or most frequent object; it is the center of the\n 205: self-colored cluster, cropped to that object's bounding box with background kept.\n 206: </description>\n 207: </reference_puzzle>\n 208: \n 209: <reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e048c9ed\" lines=\"11-26\">\n 210: <description>\n 211: Add a quantity-color label in the top marker column for each horizontal bar.\n 212: \n 213: Input structure\n 214: - The grid has a black background and one non-background marker pixel in the top row.\n 215: - Below the marker row, every non-empty source row contains one solid monochrome horizontal bar to the left of the marker column.\n 216: - Source rows are staggered every other row.\n 217: \n 218: Rule\n 219: - Copy the input grid.\n 220: - For each source bar, read its quantity as the bar length.\n\nFILE: /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/15/des.md\n   1: <new_puzzle>\n   2: - `description`：根据边框上的颜色缺口确定每个封闭区域的\"出口方向\"，再将区域内的图案沿该方向翻转后印到相邻的空白区域中。\n   3: \n   4: - `Input structure`：\n   5:   - 背景为 Black。\n   6:   - 网格中有若干由同一颜色（如 Blue）绘制的矩形边框，每个边框恰好有一个单像素宽的缺口（缺口处为 Black）。\n   7:   - 每个边框内部包含一个由其他颜色（Red、Green、Yellow 等）组成的小图案，图案不触碰边框。\n   8:   - 每个边框外部、缺口方向紧邻的位置有一块与边框内部等大的空白（Black）区域，周围没有其他对象遮挡。\n   9: \n  10: - `Rule`：\n  11:   - 对每个边框，找到其唯一缺口所在的边（上、下、左、右）。\n  12:   - 将边框内部的图案沿**垂直于缺口所在边的轴**做镜像翻转。例如：缺口在右边，则沿竖直轴左右翻转；缺口在上边，则沿水平轴上下翻转。\n  13:   - 将翻转后的图案平移到缺口外侧对应的空白区域中（偏移量恰好等于边框内部区域的宽度或高度加上边框厚度 1 像素）。\n  14:   - 原边框和内部图案保持不变。\n  15: \n  16: - `Key insight`：\n  17:   缺口方向不仅决定图案的\"输出位置\"，还隐含地决定了镜像轴——解题者需要同时归纳出\"缺口→位移方向\"和\"缺口→翻转轴\"这两条互相关联但并不显然的映射。\n  18: </new_puzzle>\n  19: \n  20: <new_puzzle>\n  21: - `description`：利用散落的单色\"钥匙\"形状与边框内部的\"锁孔\"负形进行旋转匹配，用钥匙的颜色填充对应锁孔。\n  22: \n  23: - `Input structure`：\n  24:   - 背景为 Black。\n  25:   - 网格中有若干由 Grey 绘制的矩形边框（宽度 1 像素），每个边框内部为 Azure 填充，其中挖去了一个不规则连通区域（\"锁孔\"），锁孔像素为 Black，被 Azure 填充衬托而清晰可见。\n  26:   - 网格中还散落着若干由不同颜色（Red、Green、Yellow、Magenta 等）组成的小型连通单色图案（\"钥匙\"），每个钥匙不在任何边框内部。\n  27:   - 每个钥匙的形状经旋转 0°/90°/180°/270° 之一后恰好与某个锁孔的形状完全吻合。钥匙与锁孔一一对应。\n  28: \n  29: - `Rule`：\n  30:   - 对每个边框，提取其内部 Azure 填充中的 Black 连通区域作为锁孔形状。\n  31:   - 对每个散落钥匙，尝试四种旋转，找到与某个锁孔形状完全匹配的唯一配对。\n  32:   - 用该钥匙的颜色填充对应锁孔的所有像素（替换 Black 为钥匙颜色）。\n  33:   - 钥匙本身在输出中被擦除（恢复为 Black 背景）。\n  34: \n  35: - `Key insight`：\n  36:   锁孔是负形（被填充色衬托出的空洞），钥匙是正形；解题者需要先识别出\"负形-正形\"的对应关系，再通过旋转匹配完成配对——两步都需要非平凡的视觉归纳。\n  37: </new_puzzle>\n  38: \n  39: <new_puzzle>\n  40: - `description`：根据每行\"信号灯\"的亮灭模式在图例区查表，获得该模式对应的列置换规则，然后将置换应用到操作区同行的彩色条纹上。\n  41: \n  42: - `Input structure`：\n  43:   - 网格宽度为 N+3，其中右侧 3 列为\"信号灯区\"，左侧 N 列为\"条纹区\"。两区之间无分隔。\n  44:   - 信号灯区的每一行包含 3 个像素，每个像素为 Maroon（灭）或 Yellow（亮），形成一个三位亮灭模式。\n  45:   - 条纹区的每一行包含若干不同颜色的像素（非 Black、非 Maroon、非 Yellow），构成一个彩色序列。\n  46:   - 网格中有一行完全为 Black 的分隔行，将网格分成上下两个面板：上面板是\"图例区\"，下面板是\"操作区\"。\n  47:   - 图例区中，每一行展示一种信号灯模式以及该模式下条纹区已经过变换的结果——同一行条纹区的颜色顺序即为变换后输出。图例区覆盖了操作区中出现的所有信号灯模式，每种模式恰好出现一次。\n  48:   - 操作区中，条纹区的内容是待变换的原始序列，各行的信号灯模式可以与图例区中的某行相同。\n  49: \n  50: - `Rule`：\n  51:   - 对操作区中的每一行，读取其右侧 3 个像素的亮灭组合（信号灯模式）。\n  52:   - 在图例区中找到信号灯模式相同的行。观察图例行条纹区各位置的颜色排列相对于一个标准升序参考（可从图例区所有行的对比中推断）发生了怎样的列位置置换。\n  53:   - 将同样的列位置置换应用到操作区该行的条纹像素上，得到输出行。\n  54:   - 信号灯区在输出中保持不变。\n  55: \n  56: - `Key insight`：\n  57:   信号灯模式本身不直接编码变换方式（不是简单的二进制编码）——它是一个查表索引，解题者必须先从图例区归纳出\"模式→排列置换\"的映射表，再应用到操作区。两步推理缺一不可。\n  58: </new_puzzle>\n  59: \n  60: <new_puzzle>\n  61: - `description`：通过模板区域内锚点像素的颜色与对象进行匹配，再依据锚点在模板内的空间位置确定对象的放置偏移，将对象嵌入对应模板中。\n  62: \n  63: - `Input structure`：\n  64:   - 背景为 Black。\n  65:   - 网格被一条完整的 Grey 水平线分成上下两个半区：上半区为\"模板半区\"，下半区为\"对象半区\"。\n  66:   - 模板半区中包含若干互不接触的小型连通区域，每个区域由同一种颜色填充（如 Blue、Red、Green 等），形状为简单几何形（矩形、L 形等）。每个模板区域内部恰好有一个像素的颜色与该区域主色不同——这个异色像素称为\"锚点\"，其颜色称为\"锚色\"。\n  67:   - 对象半区中包含若干互不接触的单色连通对象，每个对象颜色各不相同，且每个对象的颜色恰好等于某个模板区域的锚色。对象数量与模板数量相同，颜色一一对应。\n  68: \n  69: - `Rule`：\n  70:   - 对每个对象，通过颜色匹配找到其对应的模板区域（对象颜色 = 模板的锚色）。\n  71:   - 记录锚点在其模板区域边界框内的相对位置（行偏移、列偏移）。\n  72:   - 将对象平移至模板区域的边界框内，使对象边界框的左上角与模板边界框的左上角对齐后，再额外偏移至锚点的相对位置处（即对象的左上角与锚点位置重合）。\n  73:   - 输出仅包含模板半区的范围（裁剪掉 Grey 分隔线和对象半区）。模板区域的主色保持不变，锚点位置被对象的像素覆盖，对象中超出模板边界框的部分被裁剪。\n  74: \n  75: - `Key insight`：\n  76:   锚点同时编码了两层信息：其颜色决定\"哪个对象属于这个模板\"，其在模板内的空间位置决定\"对象放在模板的哪个位置\"。解题者需要先发现颜色匹配关系，再发现锚点的空间定位语义。\n  77: </new_puzzle>\n  78: \n  79: <new_puzzle>\n  80: - `description`：根据每个封闭房间内\"种子\"像素的数量，从颜色图例中查找对应颜色，并用该颜色填充整个房间。\n  81: \n  82: - `Input structure`：\n  83:   - 背景为 Black。\n  84:   - 网格中有由 Grey 像素绘制的连通墙壁结构，将网格内部划分为若干不规则但封闭的\"房间\"（4-连通的 Black 区域，完全被 Grey 墙壁包围，不与网格边缘的外部 Black 区域连通）。\n  85:   - 每个房间内部散布着若干个同色的\"种子\"像素（颜色为 Maroon），种子数量为 1 到 5 不等，不同房间的种子数量可以不同。\n  86:   - 网格的左上角区域有一个与墙壁结构分离的\"颜色图例\"：图例由 5 行 1 列的彩色方块组成，从上到下依次为 5 种不同颜色（如 Red、Blue、Green、Yellow、Orange），第 k 行的颜色代表种子数量 k 的映射目标。图例方块之间无间隔，纵向排成一列，图例左侧标注了行号（用与行号对应数量相同的 Maroon 像素水平排列标记，例如第 3 行左侧有 3 个 Maroon 像素）。\n  87: \n  88: - `Rule`：\n  89:   - 数出每个封闭房间内 Maroon 种子像素的数量 k（k 在 1 到 5 之间）。\n  90:   - 在颜色图例中，找到左侧 Maroon 标记数量等于 k 的那一行，该行右侧的彩色方块颜色即为该房间的填充色。\n  91:   - 将该房间内所有 Black 像素和 Maroon 种子像素统一替换为查到的填充色。\n  92:   - 墙壁（Grey）、图例区域和外部背景保持不变。\n  93: \n  94: - `Key insight`：\n  95:   房间的填充颜色不由种子本身的颜色决定（种子全为 Maroon），而是由种子的数量通过图例间接映射——解题者需要先发现\"数种子数量\"的操作，再发现图例中\"Maroon 标记数 = 种子计数\"的行对应关系，最后完成\"数量→图例行→颜色\"这条三步映射链。\n  96: </new_puzzle>\n  97: \n  98: <new_puzzle>\n  99: - `description`：识别网格中由不同颜色标记的多个\"印章\"及其关联的\"画布\"方块，将每个印章旋转至其画布边缘标记所指示的朝向后盖印到画布上。\n 100: \n 101: - `Input structure`：\n 102:   - 背景为 Black。\n 103:   - 网格中有若干对\"印章-画布\"组合，各组合彼此不接触。\n 104:   - 每个画布是一个正方形的 Grey 填充区域（例如 5×5），其四条边的正中间像素各被替换为某种非 Grey 非 Black 的颜色。其中只有一条边的中点颜色与对应印章的主色相同，称为\"匹配标记\"；其余三条边的中点颜色统一为 Azure，称为\"无关标记\"。\n 105:   - 每个印章是一个与画布内部（去掉边框后）同尺寸的方形区域，由某种特定颜色的像素组成不规则图案，图案以外为 Black 背景。印章以默认朝向放置（上方为原始上方）。印章的主色与其配对画布上匹配标记的颜色相同。\n 106: \n 107: - `Rule`：\n 108:   - 对每个画布，找到四条边中点标记中唯一与某印章主色相同的那条边——该边即\"目标边\"，同时确定印章与画布的配对关系。\n 109:   - 根据目标边相对于画布顶边的方位确定旋转角度：顶边 = 0°，右边 = 顺时针 90°，底边 = 180°，左边 = 顺时针 270°。\n 110:   - 将配对印章按上述角度旋转。\n 111:   - 将旋转后的印章图案叠加到画布的内部区域上（即画布去掉最外一圈 Grey 边框后的区域）：印章的非 Black 像素覆盖画布对应位置的 Grey 像素，印章的 Black 像素不改变画布原有内容。\n 112:   - 输出中印章原始位置被清除为 Black 背景。\n 113: \n 114: - `Key insight`：\n 115:   画布的四个边缘标记中只有一个与印章颜色匹配——这个匹配不仅确定了配对关系，还同时编码了旋转角度。解题者需要分两步归纳：先通过颜色识别出印章与画布的配对，再通过匹配标记所在的边确定旋转方向。\n 116: </new_puzzle>\n 117: \n 118: <new_puzzle>\n 119: - `description`：根据网格中\"传送门\"对的入口标记位置，将从光源发出的直线光线在传送门之间正确地转向并接续延伸。\n 120: \n 121: - `Input structure`：\n 122:   - 背景为 Black。\n 123:   - 网格中有若干对同色的\"传送门\"——每个传送门由 3 个连续的同色像素组成（水平排列或竖直排列）。同种颜色恰好出现两个传送门（即一对）。可能有多对不同颜色的传送门。\n 124:   - 每个传送门的一侧（垂直于门排列方向的相邻行或列）紧邻一个 Maroon 像素，称为\"入口标记\"。入口标记位于传送门中间像素的正旁边，指示光线从哪个方向进入或射出该传送门。\n 125:   - 网格中有一个 Yellow 像素作为\"光源\"，光源与某个传送门之间有一条无遮挡的水平或竖直直线视线。\n 126: \n 127: - `Rule`：\n 128:   - 光线从光源出发，沿着光源与最近传送门之间的直线方向前进，路径上的所有 Black 像素被绘制为 Yellow。\n 129:   - 当光线到达某个传送门的入口标记侧时，光线进入该传送门。找到该传送门的同色配对传送门。\n 130:   - 光线从配对传送门的入口标记侧射出：出射方向为从传送门中心指向入口标记的方向（即垂直于传送门排列方向、朝向入口标记所在的一侧）。\n 131:   - 光线继续沿直线前进，可能再次遇到另一个传送门并重复传送过程，直到光线到达网格边缘为止。\n 132:   - 输出网格中所有光线路径上的 Black 像素被标记为 Yellow，传送门、入口标记和光源本身保持不变。\n 133: \n 134: - `Key insight`：\n 135:   光线进入一个传送门后，不是简单地保持原方向从配对门射出，而是必须按照配对门的入口标记所指方向射出——解题者需要归纳出\"入口标记决定出射方向\"这一非直觉规则，同时理解传送门的配对由颜色决定。两层规则嵌套构成核心难度。\n 136: </new_puzzle>\n 137: \n 138: <new_puzzle>\n 139: - `description`：在由彩色线段构成的层叠网络中，根据线段的交叉遮挡关系推断深度顺序，并按照从浅到深的顺序对线段重新着色。\n 140: \n 141: - `Input structure`：\n 142:   - 背景为 Black。\n 143:   - 网格中有若干条水平或竖直的单像素宽彩色线段，每条线段由唯一的一种非 Black 颜色绘制（例如 Red、Blue、Green、Yellow、Magenta 等），各线段颜色互不相同。\n 144:   - 部分线段在交叉点处重叠。在每个交叉点，只有一条线段的颜色可见（即该线段在此处\"遮挡\"了另一条线段）。被遮挡的线段在交叉点处出现一个像素的断裂（该像素显示为遮挡者的颜色）。\n 145:   - 网格右侧有一列纵向排列的颜色样本（\"深度图例\"），从上到下排列了与线段数量相同的不同颜色方块，从上到下分别代表深度 1（最浅/最上层）到深度 N（最深/最下层）。\n 146: \n 147: - `Rule`：\n 148:   - 分析所有交叉点处的遮挡关系：如果线段 A 的颜色在交叉点可见而线段 B 在该处断裂，则 A 在 B 之上（A 比 B 浅）。\n 149:   - 由所有交叉点的遮挡关系确定线段从浅到深的完整排序（题目保证遮挡关系足以确定唯一全序）。\n 150:   - 深度排名第 k 的线段（k=1 为最浅）被重新着色为深度图例中从上到下第 k 个颜色。\n 151:   - 重新着色时，被遮挡的交叉点像素也恢复为被遮挡线段的新颜色（即输出中所有线段完整无断裂，但颜色按深度重新分配）。\n 152:   - 深度图例在输出中保持不变。\n 153: \n 154: - `Key insight`：\n 155:   解题者需要三步推理：首先识别交叉点处的断裂意味着遮挡关系；其次从多个局部遮挡关系中排出全局深度顺序；最后用深度图例的颜色序列替换原有颜色。每一步都需要非平凡的归纳。\n 156: </new_puzzle>\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
